# POST /proposal, the identical duplicate seen from the leaver (R-5 of the DS re-review): carol's
# second upload of her own leave is answered as the first, so she keeps it queued - and OpenMLS
# refuses an application message from a device whose own proposal is pending. The LAST statement,
# carol's send, is therefore meant to FAIL on her own client and never reach the instance; the Go
# test (TestAMemberProposalUploadedTwiceIsAnsweredAsTheFirst) asserts exactly that. Had the instance
# refused the retry, carol would have withdrawn her leave and sent this message as a member.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
sync carol
leave carol chat
leave carol chat
send carol chat I have left
